.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=Append Block


@Contents
$^#Append block 2.0 beta 1
$^#Copyright (c) 1995-1999 Tomasz Szkudlarek

    This  plugin  allows  you  to  save  current  Far editor
    selection  to  specified  file, or insert specified file
    to current edited file.

    To  save  block,  you  should  select  block, and choose
    ~Append block~@AppendDialog@ command from menu.

    If you want insert file, you should choose ~Insert file~@InsertDialog@
    command from menu.


@AppendDialog
$^#Append Block#
    This  command  allows  you  to  save  current Far editor
    selection to specified file.

    If  you  want  to  save block, just select it and launch
    Append Block command.

    In dialog box you may find following buttons:

    #[ Append ]#       Append block to specified file

    #[ Rewrite ]#      Rewrite specified file and save block

    #[ Temp ]#         Inserts temporary folder name

    #[ Device ]#       Open Device menu

    #[ Cancel ]#       Cancel operation

    As file name you can specify special device, for example, if you
    want to print block, you can specify as filename "PRN" or choose
    device from #Device menu#.


 #Warning#
    Sometimes Far may crash when you will try to append block to
    not existing or not ready device.

 
    ~Insert file command~@InsertDialog@
    ~About Append Block plugin~@about@


@InsertDialog
$^#Insert file#

    This   command  allows  you  to  insert  specified  file
    to current edited file.

    When  you  want  to  use  this command you should choose
    Insert  file  command and specify file or browse it from
    your disk by pressing #Browse# button

    In dialog box you may find following buttons:

    #[ Insert ]#       Insert specified file

    #[ Browse ]#       Browse file by
                     ~Open file dialog~@Openfile

    #[ Temp ]#         Inserts temporary folder name

    #[ Cancel ]#       Cancel operation


    ~Append block command~@AppendDialog
    ~About Append Block plugin~@about@

@QDirs
$^#Quick dirs

    Quick dirs allows you to remember your favorite folders.

    #"+"#      Store dir
    #"-"#      Remove dir
    #<ENTER>#  Choose dir


@Openfile
$^#Open file dialog

    Shortcuts:

    #<ENTER>#      Choose file/Enter folder
    #<BackSpace>#  Up folder
    #F2#           Change disk
    #F4#           ~Quick dirs~@QDirs@

@About
$^#About Append Block plugin
